Title: Host SDL seam: build the core against SDL2 outside macOS
Repository: boxer (https://github.com/alinebee/Boxer.git)
Date: 2026-10-01
Author: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Base-Commit: 0062fc18e154cde6cef3bf3329be4b0658597e31
Preceding-Patches: none
Problem: Boxer's DOSBox includes SDL 1.2, SDL_sound and SDL_net through macOS framework paths (#import <SDL/SDL.h>) and CoreFoundation's byte-order header. Neither exists on AROS, and the mainline SDK has no SDL 1.2 at all.
Solution: On non-Apple hosts the shim headers include one seam header, boxer_host_sdl.h, which uses SDL2 (installed in both AROS SDKs) and supplies the SDL 1.2 CD-ROM types with stubs reporting no physical drives, since SDL2 dropped that API. SDL_sound and SDL_net resolve to nothing; their users are disabled by the AROS config patch. vga_draw.cpp uses SDL_SwapLE32 instead of CFSwapInt32HostToLittle. macOS builds are unchanged. All SDL use stays behind this header so SDL3 (the preferred later target) can replace SDL2 in one place.
Platform-Scope: AROS x86_64 ABIv11 and mainline v1 (any non-Apple host); no effect on __APPLE__ builds.
Upstream-Status: local-only
Verification: 2026-10-01: scripts/build-core.sh compiles all 119 TUs of the Boxer target's Sources phase with GCC 10.5.0 for ABIv11 and mainline v1; boxer-core-smoke links on both. Not run on any guest yet. Physical CD-ROM access is untested and expected absent.
Removal-Condition: When the core moves to SDL3 or a newer DOSBox core replaces this tree.

